     "nodeId": "p27-investigation-root",
     "replacement": "When you rotate the area between two curves around an axis, you create a hollow solid:\n\nThe cross-section of this solid is an **annulus**, the region between two circles with the same centre. Consider $g(x)\\ge f(x)\\ge0$:\n\nWe add up every slice between $x=a$ and $x=b$, which is equivalent to integrating:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}V&=\\int_a^b\\pi\\bigl([g(x)]^2-[f(x)]^2\\bigr)\\,dx\\\\V&=\\pi\\int_a^b\\bigl([g(x)]^2-[f(x)]^2\\bigr)\\,dx\\end{aligned}$$",
